{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZvAsoMJyDq8Keri9knG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I have:\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a POST endpoint to cancel orders with status tracking, ensuring idempotent cancellations, blocking cancellations when a CONFIRMED shipment exists, and preventing shipment creation on CANCELLED orders.\n\n**Repository findings (path:line):**\n- Order.kt:11-16 — Order entity without status field\n- OrderController.kt:17-46 — Current endpoints (create, get, list)\n- OrderRepository.kt:11-27 — In-memory store, no methods to find by other attributes\n- Shipment.kt:9-14, 23-27 — Shipment with ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController.kt:22-56, ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27 — Shipment endpoints and store\n- ApiExceptions.kt:11-24 — ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 — ErrorCode enum currently has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses for all failures\n- GlobalExceptionHandler wraps them in ApiError envelope with code and message\n- ErrorCodes live in the ApiError.kt enum\n- Tests use @SpringBootTest, @AutoConfigureMockMvc, and MockMvc\n- Tests verify both HTTP status and error.code field in responses\n- Repositories use ConcurrentHashMap; @BeforeEach clears state\n\n**Affected files** — must touch:\n1. Order.kt — add OrderStatus enum and status field to Order\n2. OrderController.kt — add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt — add findByOrderId() method to check shipments during cancel\n4. ShipmentController.kt — check order status when creating a shipment\n5. ApiError.kt — add ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n6. OrderControllerTest.kt — add cancel endpoint tests\n7. ShipmentControllerTest.kt — add test for creating shipment on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- Atomicity: cancel must check all shipments' statuses then update order and shipments together\n- ShipmentRepository needs new query method findByOrderId()\n- Existing tests must keep passing after adding status field\n\n**Open questions:** None — requirement is unambiguous.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add an `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED. Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order, defaulting to ACTIVE. Keep CreateOrderRequest unchanged.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** — No changes needed; status is part of the Order value object.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to support checking all shipments of an order.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Add endpoint `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns 409 and changes nothing if any shipment is CONFIRMED\n   - Cancels all CREATED shipments and updates order to CANCELLED\n   - Succeeds idempotently if order is already CANCELLED (returns it unchanged)\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — In the create method, check if the order is CANCELLED and throw ConflictException with a new error code if so.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** — Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code to the ErrorCode enum.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds idempotently\n   - Cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and nothing changes\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n   - GET after cancel shows the order in CANCELLED status\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test for attempting to create a shipment on a CANCELLED order, expecting 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code.\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- **Option 1**: Store cancel status separately from Order (rejected) — adds complexity, violates single responsibility, Order should know its own status.\n- **Option 2**: Use a transaction/locking mechanism (rejected) — in-memory store doesn't need it; the logic is simple enough to reason about atomically.\n- **Option 3**: Add cancel as a separate method on OrderRepository (rejected) — the cancel logic is stateful (involves multiple entities) and belongs in the controller/service layer.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order with no CONFIRMED shipments**:\n   - Controller receives POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Controller calls repository.findById(orderId) — 404 if null\n   - Controller calls shipmentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId)\n   - Checks if any shipment status == CONFIRMED — if yes, throw ConflictException(ORDER_CONFIRMED, message) with 409\n   - Updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Updates order to CANCELLED\n   - Repository saves order and shipments\n   - Returns 200 with CANCELLED order in body\n\n2. **Cancel already CANCELLED order**:\n   - Same flow as above\n   - No CONFIRMED shipments (since it's already CANCELLED)\n   - Update order.status to CANCELLED (no-op since it already is)\n   - Return 200 with order\n\n3. **Cancel non-existent order**:\n   - repository.findById(orderId) returns null\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND, message) with 404\n\n4. **Create shipment on CANCELLED order**:\n   - ShipmentController.create() receives CreateShipmentRequest with orderId\n   - Query orderRepository.findById(orderId)\n   - If found and status == CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED, message) with 409\n   - Continue as normal otherwise\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest - cancel ACTIVE order**: Creates an order, POSTs /orders/{id}/cancel, expects 200 and body shows status=CANCELLED\n2. **OrderControllerTest - cancel CANCELLED order**: Cancels once, cancels again, expects 200 and no error\n3. **OrderControllerTest - cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment**: Creates order + CONFIRMED shipment, attempts cancel, expects 409 with code and unchanged state\n4. **OrderControllerTest - cancel non-existent order**: POSTs /orders/missing/cancel, expects 404 with error code\n5. **OrderControllerTest - GET after cancel shows status**: Cancel then GET, verify status is CANCELLED\n6. **OrderControllerTest - cancel CREATED shipments**: Create order + CREATED shipment, cancel, verify shipment status becomes CANCELLED\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest - create shipment on cancelled order**: Cancel an order, attempt to create shipment for it, expect 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll write the code, starting with the Order entity to add status:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1374,"cache_read_input_tokens":21678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1374},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"908ff251-ad82-4d2b-af6a-aa688c795f60","uuid":"b03bdb50-2d94-44cf-910b-409f8a0b9683","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:12:04.177Z","request_id":"req_011CfZvAsR2wZXXuqsZwJ2Q3"}
