 handles idempotent cancellation. Necessary for the feature.\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — ✅ Added findByOrderId() method to query shipments by order. Necessary to check shipment statuses during cancellation.\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — ✅ Added OrderRepository injection and check in create() method to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders with 409. Necessary per requirement.\n5. **ApiError.kt** — ✅ Added ORDER_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED error codes. Necessary for consistent error handling.\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — ✅ Added 6 new tests covering all cancel scenarios: active cancel, idempotent cancel, CONFIRMED shipment blocking cancel, non-existent order, CREATED shipment cancellation, and status verification.\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — ✅ Added 1 new test for rejecting shipment creation on cancelled order, and cleared shipmentRepository in reset.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met, all tests pass, and no unrelated changes were made.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel with ACTIVE/CANCELLED status, idempotent cancellation, CONFIRMED shipment blocking, and prevention of shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — added OrderStatus enum and status field with ACTIVE default\n              OrderController.kt — added cancel endpoint with shipment status checking and update logic\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId() query method\n              ShipmentController.kt — added order CANCELLED check when creating shipments\n              ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — added 6 tests for cancel functionality\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 1 test for rejected shipment on cancelled order\n\nTests         OrderControllerTest: cancels active order (200, CANCELLED status)\n              OrderControllerTest: idempotent cancellation (repeat cancel succeeds)\n              OrderControllerTest: non-existent order (404, ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n              OrderControllerTest: CONFIRMED shipment blocking cancel (409, SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED, no changes)\n              OrderControllerTest: CREATED shipments cancelled during order cancel\n              OrderControllerTest: GET after cancel shows CANCELLED status\n              ShipmentControllerTest: rejected shipment on cancelled order (409, ORDER_CANCELLED)\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, Tests run: 20, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\n              - OrderControllerTest: 10 tests (4 original + 6 new), all pass\n              - ShipmentControllerTest: 6 tests (5 original + 1 new), all pass\n\nNot done      Nothing — all acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, no unrelated changes.\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":669,"cache_read_input_tokens":42691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":669},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"908ff251-ad82-4d2b-af6a-aa688c795f60","uuid":"2e81648b-15c2-4687-ad47-a4e7e8a8e9e9","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:14:14.241Z","request_id":"req_011CfZvMCZVpcDhZcTfYxXUg"}
